# shell: desktop
# DB-002: below the fixed head the leaf menu shows the recent lists, then
# the live contents of the Deskbar folder.  It was a compile-time array of
# ten strings, so nothing the user did could ever appear in it.
wait 8
note two folders opened, so both are in the recent list
click-row 0
wait 2
click-row 0
wait 10
expect-windows 2
note and both closed again, so what reopens one can only be the menu
key w ctrl
wait 3
key w ctrl
wait 3
expect-windows 0
click 980 20
wait 3
note the recents row EXPANDS rather than choosing: the menu stays up
expect-menu About this system|Find…|Deskbar preferences…|Tracker preferences…|Show replicants|Applications|-|/sys|/dev|/data|-|Recent folders|-|<Deskbar folder is empty>|-|Shut down…|
menu-pick Recent folders
wait 3
expect-windows 0
note and its entry opens the folder it names
note the row expanded: the folders just opened are BESIDE the leaf menu
expect-menu About this system|Find…|Deskbar preferences…|Tracker preferences…|Show replicants|Applications|-|/sys|/dev|/data|-|Recent folders|-|<Deskbar folder is empty>|-|Shut down…|sub|trk_script|
menu-pick sub
wait 8
expect-windows 1
expect-title sub
quit
